From: EBDS Tecnologia Ltda.
Subject: [PATCH] asn1c: make the generated codec compile with MSVC

asn1c 0.9.28 predates MSVC 2010 and carries two assumptions that break a
modern cl.exe build.  Both fixes are confined to Windows/MSVC preprocessor
branches, so the generated tree stays byte-identical for every other
toolchain and the patch can be applied unconditionally at generation time.

1. asn_internal.h uses a bare __attribute__((unused)) on
   ASN__STACK_OVERFLOW_CHECK instead of the GCC_NOTUSED macro that
   asn_system.h defines exactly for this purpose (and which already expands
   to nothing on non-GCC compilers).

2. asn_system.h, under _WIN32:
   - aliases snprintf/vsnprintf to _snprintf/_vsnprintf.  Those do not
     NUL-terminate on truncation.  asn_system.h is included well beyond
     libasn (libipa, ipa, the tests), so on MSVC 2015+ this would silently
     downgrade every snprintf() in the project -- including the
     bounds-checked path build in main.c.  Restrict the alias to the
     toolchains that actually lack the C99 functions.
   - typedefs int8_t..uint32_t itself, with int8_t as plain `char`.  The
     CRT's <stdint.h> uses `signed char`, making this a hard redefinition
     error (C2371) on MSVC 2010+.  Use the standard header there instead
     and take ssize_t from SSIZE_T.
---
--- a/src/ipa/libasn/asn_internal.h
+++ b/src/ipa/libasn/asn_internal.h
@@ -104,7 +104,7 @@
  * Check stack against overflow, if limit is set.
  */
 #define	ASN__DEFAULT_STACK_MAX	(30000)
-static int __attribute__((unused))
+static int GCC_NOTUSED
 ASN__STACK_OVERFLOW_CHECK(asn_codec_ctx_t *ctx) {
 	if(ctx && ctx->max_stack_size) {
 
--- a/src/ipa/libasn/asn_system.h
+++ b/src/ipa/libasn/asn_system.h
@@ -32,8 +32,15 @@
 #ifdef	_WIN32
 
 #include <malloc.h>
+/* MSVC 2015 (_MSC_VER 1900) and later provide C99-conformant snprintf() and
+ * vsnprintf(); MinGW always did.  The legacy _snprintf/_vsnprintf do NOT
+ * NUL-terminate on truncation, so aliasing to them on a modern toolchain
+ * silently downgrades every snprintf() in the project -- asn_system.h is
+ * pulled in far beyond libasn.  Alias only where it is actually needed. */
+#if defined(_MSC_VER) && _MSC_VER < 1900
 #define	 snprintf	_snprintf
 #define	 vsnprintf	_vsnprintf
+#endif
 
 /* To avoid linking with ws2_32.lib, here's the definition of ntohl() */
 #define sys_ntohl(l)	((((l) << 24)  & 0xff000000)	\
@@ -45,6 +52,22 @@
 #ifndef __cplusplus
 #define inline __inline
 #endif
+#if _MSC_VER >= 1600
+/* MSVC 2010 and later ship a C99 <stdint.h>.  The legacy typedefs below would
+ * collide with it -- int8_t as plain `char` against the CRT's `signed char` is
+ * a hard redefinition error (C2371) -- so take the standard header instead and
+ * get ssize_t from SSIZE_T in <BaseTsd.h>. */
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <BaseTsd.h>
+#ifndef	_SSIZE_T_DEFINED
+#define	_SSIZE_T_DEFINED
+typedef SSIZE_T ssize_t;
+#endif
+#ifndef	ASSUMESTDTYPES
+#define	ASSUMESTDTYPES	1
+#endif
+#endif	/* _MSC_VER >= 1600 */
+
 #ifndef	ASSUMESTDTYPES	/* Standard types have been defined elsewhere */
 #define	ssize_t		SSIZE_T
 typedef	char		int8_t;
